<p>I actually want to clarify on a couple points you've made here. Harkand isn't dead, neither is Martin, or Brendan. None of them are dead, however I didn't want to outright state that within the article, so I put some very subtle details into the logs that may or may not have been easy to pick up on (some people have gotten it right away after reading, others haven't which is fine).</p>
<p>I juggled a delicate balance while writing this, I <em>wanted</em> to include an additional set of logs as I described in my response to Roget and the original discussion post, but based on the general feedback I received It felt more and more like an additional log would just take away from effect of the Journals. Perhaps once the 3000 contest has ended I will reevaluate this, and instead add an additional log straight in.</p>
<p>Also, to clarify, they aren't being transported to an additional dimension. This isn't extra dimensional. Wherever the Nuckelavees come from, it's still on Earth.</p>
<p>As an aside, is there anything you think I could do with the WWI logs that would help make it less anticlimactic?</p>

